# Provenance of rtl/snac_psx.v, which is copied from the repo below.
#
# This module is NOT canonical here. It is copied from FringeCoder/AmigaCD, the
# userspace repo, which owns it -- see rtl/README.md there, and the module's own
# header. Do not fix a bug in the copy: fix it there, then re-vendor, or the
# copies silently diverge and the next sync quietly reverts you.
#
# Three repositories carry this file: FringeCoder/AmigaCD (canonical),
# FringeCoder/Menu_MiSTer and this one. The two core copies are checked against
# this stamp rather than against each other, because a check between the cores
# would pass while both drifted away from the file they were taken from.
#
# CI checks the local file against the sha256 below. If that step fails, either
# the copy was edited in place (don't) or a re-vendor updated the file and not
# this stamp. Procedure: rtl/README.md in the FringeCoder/AmigaCD repo.
#
# There is no bench for this module in this repository -- it lives in
# FringeCoder/Menu_MiSTer (rtl/sim/snac_psx/), which is where the reader was
# brought up because the Menu core fits in a quarter of the time. Run it there
# after a re-vendor; this stamp only proves the bytes match, not that they work.
#
# Refresh with: ./snac_vendor_check.sh --stamp /path/to/amigacd-checkout

